2269 |             Criterion to apply to each group. Should return True or False.\n2270 |         dropna : bool\n2271 |             Drop groups that do not pass the filter. True by default; if False,\n2272 |             groups that evaluate False are filled with NaNs.\n2273 |         *args : tuple\n2274 |             Additional positional arguments to pass to `func`.\n2275 |         **kwargs : dict\n2276 |             Additional keyword arguments to pass to `func`.\n2277 | \n2278 |         Returns\n2279 |         -------\n2280 |         DataFrame\n2281 |             The filtered subset of the original DataFrame.\n2282 | \n2283 |         See Also\n2284 |         --------\n2285 |         DataFrame.filter: Filter elements of ungrouped DataFrame.\n2286 |         SeriesGroupBy.filter : Filter elements from groups base on criterion.\n2287 | \n2288 |         Notes\n2289 |         -----\n2290 |         Each subframe is endowed the attribute 'name' in case you need to know\n2291 |         which group you are working on.\n2292 | \n2293 |         Functions that mutate the passed object can produce unexpected\n2294 |         behavior or errors and are not supported. See :ref:`gotchas.udf-mutation`\n2295 |         for more details.\n2296 | \n2297 |         Examples\n2298 |         --------\n2299 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame(\n2300 |         ...     {\n2301 |         ...         \"A\": [\"foo\", \"bar\", \"foo\", \"bar\", \"foo\", \"bar\"],\n2302 |         ...         \"B\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6],\n2303 |         ...         \"C\": [2.0, 5.0, 8.0, 1.0, 2.0, 9.0],\n2304 |         ...     }\n2305 |         ... )\n2306 |         >>> grouped = df.groupby(\"A\")\n2307 |         >>> grouped.filter(lambda x: x[\"B\"].mean() > 3.0)\n2308 |              A  B    C\n2309 |         1  bar  2  5.0\n2310 |         3  bar  4  1.0\n2311 |         5  bar  6  9.0\n2312 |         \"\"\"\n2313 |         indices = []\n2314 | \n2315 |         obj = self._selected_obj\n2316 |         gen = self._groupe